From 36f829da8bc1396e8c8198e3c2e0c147c78d14ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Constantin <fokouaconstantin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 21:21:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ple: read the n-gram table at full BF16 precision

The table reaches the engine as IQ4_NL (ISTA-DASLab's shard 2), which is
about 8% off per row against the checkpoint's own values. tools/ple_table_pack
already recovers Qwen's F8 E4M3 release exactly; the full checkpoint stores the
same shards as BF16, which is the source of record and 102.4 GB rather than
51.2 GB.

So accept it rather than re-quantize it. A bfloat16 IS the top half of a
float32, so widening is a shift: exact for every value, no rounding and no
scale, where casting BF16 to FP8 would carry a 3-bit mantissa and land within a
few percent of the IQ4_NL table this is meant to replace.

  - ngram: PLE_ROW_BYTES_BF16 (320) and bf16_dequant_row, widening little-endian
    bytes explicitly so the result does not depend on host endianness.
  - PleTable::open: a BF16 tensor sets the row width; it needs no scale and
    trusts no metadata, because the values carry themselves.
  - The direct reader takes the table's own row size, so BF16 reads unbuffered
    like IQ4_NL and FP8 instead of falling back to the mapped path Q5_0 needs.
    The comment claiming fixed 90-byte rows was stale from before FP8.
  - tools/ple_fp8_pack.py -> tools/ple_table_pack.py: reads whichever dtype the
    checkpoint holds and copies the bytes through. FP8 output is unchanged, byte
    for byte; nothing imports or tests the old path, so the rename is free.
  - ple_reader_test: the widening is exact over the patterns a lossy path breaks
    on (subnormals, +-inf, both NaNs), and a synthetic BF16 GGUF reads back
    identically through Direct and Mmap. Both were mutation-checked - widening by
    >> instead of <<, and a 160 B row width, both fail the selftest.

Host build and ple_reader_selftest pass. No GPU, model or engine run: this says
the reader widens BF16 exactly, not that a 102 GB table serves prompts well.

(cherry picked from commit 33a2775a6a9ff912d90054bd6e40b878dbe5bc05)
(cherry picked from commit 4ae54787d69f5ed30c97907739438d9a20dddafd)
